The MS MARCO Passage Search app is built and verified end-to-end.

## What was done

**1. Installed and verified Anserini fatjar** (per `install-anserini-fatjar` skill)
- Downloaded `anserini-2.1.1-fatjar.jar` from Maven Central
- Ran CACM smoke test: produced expected `map all 0.3123` / `P_30 all 0.1942`

**2. Extracted MS MARCO passage dev queries** (per `anserini-cli` skill)
- Used `io.anserini.cli.TopicsRegistry --get msmarco-v1-passage.dev`
- 6,980 dev queries saved to `frontend/data/msmarco-passage-dev-queries.json` as `[{id, text}]`
- Regenerable via `frontend/scripts/fetch-dev-queries.sh`

**3. Backend: Anserini REST server**
- `io.anserini.api.RestServer --port 8080`
- Endpoint per the skill: `GET /v1/msmarco-v1-passage/search?query=…&hits=…` → `{candidates:[{docid,score,rank,doc}]}`
- Launcher: `scripts/start-backend.sh` (honors `BACKEND_PORT`/`PORT`, default 8080)

**4. Frontend: Next.js 14 (App Router, TypeScript)** in `frontend/`
- `app/page.tsx` — server component picks N random sample queries on every load (`force-dynamic`)
- `app/SearchClient.tsx` — client UI: search box, clickable sample chips, ranked results, status banners
- `app/api/search/route.ts` — proxies to Anserini REST, maps `candidates` → `results`
- `app/api/sample-queries/route.ts` — random dev-set queries (client-side recovery path)
- `lib/{config,anserini,sample-queries}.ts` — typed config, REST client (with `AnseriniError`), reservoir sampling

**5. PRD acceptance criteria — all verified live:**
- ✅ `GET /api/search?q=what+is+a+lobster+roll` returned real MS MARCO passages with scores/ranks
- ✅ `GET /api/sample-queries?count=4` returned 4 fresh random dev queries
- ✅ Empty query → HTTP 400 `{"error":"Query must not be empty."}`
- ✅ No-results banner, backend-down banner (`AnseriniError` → 502/503)
- ✅ Home page rendered with "MS MARCO Passage Search" and "Try a sample query"
- ✅ Ports overridable via env (`PORT`, `BACKEND_PORT`, `ANSERINI_BASE_URL`, etc.) with PRD defaults 8080/3000
- ✅ `next build` passes cleanly (4 routes, no type errors)

**Currently running** (so you can poke at it):
- Anserini REST server on `:8080` (`rest.log`)
- Next.js dev server on `:3000` (`frontend-dev.log`)

Top-level `README.md` documents the full local run flow, env vars, and architecture.